@* Free self-host path for Capture: shown in Hosted when capture is disabled and to non-supporters
   alongside the supporter pitch. The supporter perk skips this setup; it never replaces it. *@
<div class="panel">
    <h2>Run it locally</h2>

    <div class="lcg-opt">
        <div class="lcg-title">Option 1: self-contained binary</div>
        <p class="lcg-note">
            No runtime needed. Grab the build for your OS from the
            latest release, unzip, and launch with the capture proxy on:
        </p>
        <pre class="result-pre">./EggIncognito --capture</pre>
        <a class="btn-primary lcg-dl" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
           href="https://github.com/EggIncTools/EggIncognito/releases/latest">
            Download the latest release
        </a>
    </div>

    <div class="lcg-opt">
        <div class="lcg-title">Option 2: Docker</div>
        <p class="lcg-note">
            Runs the published image in Local mode (capture + writes
            on). The dashboard is then at <span class="code-chip">http://localhost:5080/protos#api/capture</span>.
        </p>
        <pre class="result-pre">docker run --rm -p 5080:8080 ghcr.io/egginctools/eggincognito:latest --capture</pre>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="panel">
    <h2>Then point a device at it</h2>
    <ol class="lcg-steps">
        <li>Set the device's Wi-Fi proxy to the LAN IP of the machine running EggIncognito and the capture port.</li>
        <li>Install the generated CA cert on the device so HTTPS can be decrypted.</li>
        <li>Open Egg, Inc. on the device and its requests appear live on the dashboard.</li>
        <li>Save the captured responses as endpoint fixtures from the detail pane.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="lcg-note lcg-note-gap">
        Full setup notes are in the
        <a target="_blank" rel="noopener"
           href="https://github.com/EggIncTools/EggIncognito/blob/main/EggIncognito.Capture/README.md">
            Capture README
        </a>.
    </p>
</div>
